# Signal vs continuum classification with Belle II event-shape features

**{{course}} (Project 1) - {{institution}}.** Student: {{student_name}} ({{roll}}).

**Question.** How well can {{n_feat}} Belle II event-shape features separate **signal** (`type = +1`) from **continuum background** (`type = 0` or `-1`), which classifier is best, and how much can the feature set be reduced?

> **Label mapping.** The code meanings come from the instructor's clarification relayed by the student (type +1 = signal; type 0 or -1 = continuum; codes 2-5 = other decays). It cannot be verified from the data files. Codes 2-5 are neither category, so I excluded them from this experiment - an *analysis decision*, not an instructor instruction. The CSV contains **{{n_signal}} signal, {{n_continuum}} continuum (all type 0) and {{n_minus1}} type -1 rows**; none were invented. The sample is {{sig_frac}} signal, so accuracy alone is misleading (predict-all-signal scores {{maj_acc}}).

