## Data

`data/raw/data_hep.csv` - {{n_rows_total}} rows, {{n_feat}} numeric features, an unnamed index-like column, and `type` (counts {{type_counts}}). SHA-256 `{{csv_sha}}`. Provided by the course as the Belle II sample; provenance not independently verified. **The CSV is git-ignored** (80 MB; permission to redistribute is not established): place your copy at `data/raw/data_hep.csv`. The index-like column repeats values and its range depends on the label; its origin is undocumented, so it is excluded from predictors as a leakage risk. Primary experiment = `raw["type"].isin([1, 0, -1])`; excluded rows ({{excluded_by_code}}) and original row identifiers are recorded in `artifacts/metrics/split_assignments.csv`.

